title: 'bags-list: fix on_idle cursor skipping nodes on weight exhaustion'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `Pallet::on_idle`'s auto-rebag cursor resumed from a count-based split (`accounts[rebag_budget]`)
    computed before the per-item loop ran, so it skipped past nodes the weight meter or a lock
    stopped the loop from actually reaching.

    The cursor now resumes from `accounts[max(processed, pending_len)]`, a pure index computed
    after the loop from how far it actually got and how many pending entries led the batch. No
    extra storage reads, and no risk of mismatching an account that legitimately appears in both
    `PendingRebag` and `ListNodes` at once.
crates:
- name: pallet-bags-list
  bump: patch
